.SH "NAME"
pcre2_jit_stack_assign \- assign stack for JIT matching
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.sp
.ss \n[.ss]
.nf
.fam C
\f(CR\&#include <pcre2.h>

void\fP \f(CBpcre2_jit_stack_assign\fP\f(CR(pcre2_match_context *\fP\f(CImcontext\fP\f(CR,
                            pcre2_jit_callback\fP \f(CIcallback\fP\f(CR,
                            void *\fP\f(CIcallback_data\fP\f(CR);\fP
.fam
.fi
.ss \n[.ss] 0
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.sp
This function provides control over the memory used by JIT as a run\-time stack
when \f(CBpcre2_match()\fP or \f(CBpcre2_jit_match()\fP is called with a pattern
that has been successfully processed by the JIT compiler. The information that
determines which stack is used is put into a match context that is subsequently
passed to a matching function. The arguments of this function are:
.sp
.RS 4
.PD 0
.TP 14
\f(CImcontext\fP
.ad l
a pointer to a match context
.TP 14
\f(CIcallback\fP
.ad l
a callback function
.TP 14
\f(CIcallback_data\fP
.ad l
a JIT stack or a value to be passed to the callback
.PD
.RE
.PP
.ad l
.sp
If \f(CImcontext\fP is \f(CBNULL\fP, the function returns immediately, without doing
anything.
.sp
If \f(CIcallback\fP is \f(CBNULL\fP and \f(CIcallback_data\fP is \f(CBNULL\fP, an internal block of 32KiB
on the machine stack is used.
.sp
If \f(CIcallback\fP is \f(CBNULL\fP and \f(CIcallback_data\fP is not \f(CBNULL\fP,
\f(CIcallback_data\fP must be a valid JIT stack, the result of calling
\f(CBpcre2_jit_stack_create()\fP.
.sp
If \f(CIcallback\fP not \f(CBNULL\fP, it is called with \f(CIcallback_data\fP as an
argument at the start of matching, in order to set up a JIT stack. If the
result is \f(CBNULL\fP, the internal stack of 32KiB is used; otherwise the return value
must be a valid JIT stack, the result of calling
\f(CBpcre2_jit_stack_create()\fP.
.sp
You may safely use the same JIT stack for multiple patterns, as long as they
are all matched in the same thread. In a multithread application, each thread
must use its own JIT stack. For more details, see the
\f(CRpcre2jit\fP
page.
.sp
There is a complete description of the PCRE2 native API in the
\f(CRpcre2api\fP
page and a description of the POSIX API in the
\f(CRpcre2posix\fP
page.